====Usage notes====
Most Islamic countries nowadays use Islamic law only for civil law, chiefly family law. In such systems a qadi is accordingly a particular kind of civil judge, but this situation is recent. Typically under the Turkish form {{m|en|kadi}}, the qadis of the Ottoman Empire also initially administered the functions of all local imperial government including taxation and military conscription.

